	A while back, I asked here if people were bored with Sokoban 
(especially because there are so few puzzles to choose from). Today, 
while I was doing Sokoban for the Nth time, I thought of an idea. 
Replace Sokoban with Sudoku. The game would generate a random puzzle so 
it would be different every time (increasing in difficulty for each of 
the four levels). I'm picturing a room kinda like a 9x9 Sudoku puzzle. 
The initial clue numbers would be filled in. At the entrance, there 
would be like 500 zorkmids. You pick them up. You solve the puzzle by 
dropping gold pieces. For example, you drop 4 gold pieces into a square 
if you think the correct number is 4. If you were correct, the game 
would turn that square to '4' character (which is kinda cheating but oh 
well). I'm not sure if this would work since I didn't think of all the 
details but I think with some tuning it would be workable. I'm sure 
people would come up with better ideas. What do you guys think?


